= Labour Disputes

IG Metall and the employers in the metal and electrical industry are deadlocked. The employers want a zero round and more flexible working hours, while the union is calling warning strikes across the country. Both sides look to the labour ministry.

- @support_labor: Back the union's demands.
- @support_employers: Back the employers.
- @balance: Try to broker a compromise.
- @easy_discard

@support_labor
subtitle: Popular with the workers, but the employers will not forget it.
on-arrival: labor_strength += 5; labor_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; fdp_relation -= 4; capital_strike_progress += 1 if fdp_relation <= 30; capital_strike_progress += 1 if unemployment_rate > 8; capital_strike_progress += 1 if unemployment_rate > 11; labor_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.1; pro_labor += 1; strike_term_seen += 1; economic_growth -= 0.1;

We publicly back the union and extend collective agreements to the whole sector. The unions are pleased, while our partners on the centre-right accuse us of meddling in free collective bargaining.

@support_employers
subtitle: Popular with business, much less so with the workers.
on-arrival: labor_dissent += 8; workers_spd -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; fdp_relation += 5; cdu_relation += 5; workers_linke += 3; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 8; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 8; pro_labor -= 1; strike_term_seen += 1

We call on the union to accept wage restraint for the sake of jobs. Union members ask what the SPD is for, and the Linke is quick to answer.

@balance
subtitle: Both sides need to share the pain in the current crisis.
on-arrival: labor_dissent += 4; workers_spd -= 2; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 5; strike_term_seen += 1

A mediator brokers a deal: a modest pay rise, a one-off payment, and job guarantees at the largest plants. Nobody celebrates, but the strikes end.
